1
00:40:57,525 --> 00:41:00,058
That clock hasn't struck the
hour in the last 10 years...

2
00:41:00,088 --> 00:41:02,349
if I'm to believe what
Mark Fleming told me.

3
00:41:02,515 --> 00:41:04,369
Why is it angled away
from the wall like that?

4
00:41:04,399 --> 00:41:06,826
I don't know. Somebody must've moved it.

5
00:41:07,278 --> 00:41:10,565
- Lizzie, very like when she was dusting.
- Wait a minute.

6
00:41:11,152 --> 00:41:13,081
Did you know there's
a door in this paneling?

7
00:41:13,111 --> 00:41:17,371
No, I didn't. Oh, by gracious, so there is.

8
00:41:17,401 --> 00:41:21,138
- Maybe it opens to a secret passage.
- Certainly to a secret something!

9
00:41:21,741 --> 00:41:25,253
Who knows girls, we may be about
to stumble on that missing million.

10
00:41:26,859 --> 00:41:30,610
Oh, there's a panel, there must
be some gimmick to it, there always is.

11
00:41:44,845 --> 00:41:48,242
Calling car 11, calling car 11.

12
00:41:49,261 --> 00:41:54,849
Proceed to the Oaks in Zenith township
immediately, a homicide is been reported.

13
00:41:56,274 --> 00:41:59,670
Ok, proceeding to the Oaks.

14
00:42:00,157 --> 00:42:04,487
Notify the county coroner, Dr. Wells.
Tell him to come to the Oaks at once.

15
00:42:14,646 --> 00:42:15,379
Horrible.

16
00:42:16,219 --> 00:42:20,850
It's as if his throat had been torn
by some creature with fans or claws.

17
00:42:21,359 --> 00:42:22,517
That's his sign.

18
00:42:23,312 --> 00:42:24,972
We found it on the others he killed.

19
00:42:26,639 --> 00:42:28,649
I'd hoped those reports
that he was up to his

20
00:42:28,673 --> 00:42:30,683
old tricks again were
pure imagination but...

21
00:42:31,578 --> 00:42:33,322
apparently they're based on fact.

22
00:42:34,642 --> 00:42:35,591
He's come back...

23
00:42:36,756 --> 00:42:38,670
back to the scene of his kills.

24
00:42:40,738 --> 00:42:41,981
Yes, that's who I mean.

25
00:42:42,985 --> 00:42:44,119
That's who did this.

26
00:42:45,524 --> 00:42:46,388
The Bat.

27
00:42:47,894 --> 00:42:50,171
- Who found Mark?
- We all did.

28
00:42:51,043 --> 00:42:54,756
That is Dale and Judie and I,
Lizzie was in the dining room.

29
00:42:55,104 --> 00:42:59,195
This is my new housekeeper, Jane Patterson.
You know, she worked for John Fleming.

30
00:42:59,342 --> 00:43:00,044
I know her.

31
00:43:00,747 --> 00:43:02,113
Where were you Miss Patterson?

32
00:43:02,452 --> 00:43:04,351
In the kitchen, cleaning up.

33
00:43:05,176 --> 00:43:06,843
I cooked the dinner tonight.

34
00:43:07,365 --> 00:43:09,898
Did you know that this
secret closet was here?

35
00:43:10,670 --> 00:43:13,227
No, it was behind
the grandfather's clock.

36
00:43:13,251 --> 00:43:15,808
Well, it was I
who found it, really.

37
00:43:15,991 --> 00:43:19,881
Noticed the clock had been moved
and the door wasn't quite closed.

38
00:43:20,318 --> 00:43:21,343
I'll get it.

39
00:43:35,362 --> 00:43:36,373
Who is it?

40
00:43:45,056 --> 00:43:46,473
Mark Fleming.

41
00:43:47,271 --> 00:43:50,030
As coroner, you saw the
same wounds on the others.

42
00:43:51,146 --> 00:43:54,070
- How long is he been dead?
- Oh, I'd say about a half an hour.

43
00:43:54,661 --> 00:43:58,262
- You believe it was the Bat?
- That's the Bat's trademark.

44
00:43:59,121 --> 00:44:03,236
- Perhaps he's still in the house.
- It's possible.

45
00:44:06,975 --> 00:44:08,106
Why should he be?

46
00:44:08,621 --> 00:44:11,965
Because he's looking for something
and like you, he believes it's here.

47
00:44:12,596 --> 00:44:14,558
And he's a persistent killer.

48
00:44:14,588 --> 00:44:17,648
I would advise you
get out of this house as quickly as possible.

49
00:44:17,859 --> 00:44:20,784
Not withstanding
our expert police protection.

50
00:44:21,703 --> 00:44:23,754
- Have you called the morgue?
- They're on their way here.

51
00:44:23,784 --> 00:44:26,437
Oh, good, I want to examine
the body before they get here.
